course: dictionary
lesson: 12378
title: Crystalline: clear, bright and made of crystals
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Crystalline sounds like the word crystal, and it is built the same way. A crystal is a solid with a neat, regular shape, so crystalline means made of crystals, or having the same neat, repeating pattern. The word can be used in science, in stories, and in talk about sound.
explain: Read the words around it to find the meaning. «The lake was crystalline in the early sunlight.» You can see the bottom of the lake and the light is sparkling, so crystalline must mean very clear and bright. Try your meaning in the sentence: "The lake was very clear and bright in the early sunlight." That makes sense.
explain: In science, «Salt is a crystalline solid.» Here the word has a exact meaning: the tiny particles in salt are arranged in a neat pattern that repeats again and again. That pattern is why salt grains have flat faces and sharp edges. In stories, the same word can describe a bright voice: «Her voice was crystalline.» Then it means very clear and pure, not made of anything.
fact: Crystalline means made of crystals, or having the regular, repeating structure of a crystal.
fact: «Crystalline» also means very clear, bright and sparkling, like crystal, as in «crystalline water».
fact: For sound or speech, «crystalline» means very clear and pure, as in «a crystalline voice».
fact: Salt, sugar, quartz, ice and snowflakes are all crystalline substances.
fact: A good check is to swap in "clear and sparkling" or "made of crystals" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «Salt is a crystalline solid.» In science, what does crystalline mean here? | Hot enough to melt | Soft and bendy | Full of air bubbles | *Made of crystals, with particles in a neat repeating pattern
exercise: «The lake was crystalline in the early sunlight.» What does crystalline suggest? | Empty of water | *Very clear and sparkling | Noisy and rough | Dark and muddy
exercise: Ava says «a crystalline voice» means a voice that is muffled. What does it really mean? | Hoarse from shouting | Quiet and muffled | Loud and rough | *Very clear and pure
test: «Sugar grains look crystalline under a magnifying glass.» What shape do crystalline solids usually have? | *Flat faces and sharp edges | Round like a ball | Soft and floppy | Stretchy like elastic
test: Which of these is a crystalline solid? | Smoke | Mud | *Ice | Oil
exam: Mia says «crystalline» means cloudy, like milk. Is she right? | *No, it means very clear and bright, like crystal | Yes, cloudy is right | Yes, it means cold and wet | No, it means dark and heavy
